---
import Prose from './Prose.astro';
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro';
import { DEPLOY_BEST_PRACTICES } from '../data/guide';
---

<Prose class="max-w-none">
  <h3>How TechCart deploys</h3>
  <p>
    The backend runs on Render as a Docker service, built from docker/Dockerfile.backend through the
    repo-root render.yaml Blueprint, and redeploys on merge to main. The buyer and admin apps are
    two separate Vercel projects pointed at the same repository, each with its project root
    directory set to its workspace folder; every pull request gets a preview deployment.
  </p>
  <p>
    There are three isolated environments — development, staging and production — and each has its
    own MongoDB Atlas cluster and its own Razorpay key pair. For local work, one command brings the
    whole stack up:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="terminal"
    code={'docker compose up --build\n# backend :4000  buyer-app :3000  admin-app :5173'}
  />

  <h3>Best practices</h3>
  <ul>
    {DEPLOY_BEST_PRACTICES.map((practice) => (
      <li>{practice}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h3>This landing page</h3>
  <p>
    Simpler: astro build produces a static dist/ folder, Vercel auto-detects the Astro framework
    preset, and no configuration is needed. A vercel.json is only required for custom headers or
    redirects, and any static host works as a fallback.
  </p>
</Prose>
